BlueNetplay includes or builds on the following third-party work.

drivers/
  Linux driver for the I-O DATA GV-USB2, reworked from GV-USB2-Driver by
  Isaac Lozano (https://github.com/Isaac-Lozano/GV-USB2-Driver).
  Copyright (c) 2019 Isaac Lozano. Dual-licensed under the BSD-3-Clause
  license and the GNU General Public License version 2; see
  drivers/LICENSE.bsd and drivers/LICENSE.gpl. The changes are described in
  drivers/README.md.

tests/test_gamepad_sim.py, tests/test_ble_sim.py
  Contain Python ports of parts of BlueRetro (SDP parser, HID report
  descriptor parser, N64 button mapping) by Jacques Gagnon
  (https://github.com/darthcloud/BlueRetro), licensed under the Apache
  License, Version 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).
  The Bluetooth gamepads in gamepad.py and ble_pads.py follow what
  BlueRetro's source expects from a controller.

Dependencies (not included, installed separately):
  Bumble (https://github.com/google/bumble), Apache License 2.0
  aiohttp (https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp), Apache License 2.0
  FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org), LGPL 2.1+ / GPL 2+ depending on the build
